  "output": "The series plan file is written.\n\n## What changed\n\nCreated `.benzene/material/marketing/video/youtube-2026-10-26-frontend-terms-series.md` — a YouTube Short series plan with **12 video entries**, one per term across the UI, State and Server layers of the Universal Frontend Architecture.\n\nEach entry follows the `youtube` skill format exactly:\n- Front matter: `channel: youtube`, `date`, `format: short`, `aspect: \"9:16\"`, `duration_s` (30–60), title ≤ 100 chars, `tags` (≤ 500 chars total), `claim`, `source`, `campaign`, and a `showcase_url` on `elegantfrontend.training` tagged `utm_source=youtube&utm_medium=video&utm_campaign=<campaign>`.\n- Body: `# <title>`, then the YouTube description (showcase_url on its own line within the first two lines, ≤ 3 hashtags at the end), `## Shots` table (≥ 4 timed shots from 0 s to `duration_s` with no gaps, first shot a hook, last shot a CTA, captions ≤ 60 chars), and `## Script` line by line matching the shots.\n\nClaims are grounded in sources I read (no invented facts):\n- **UI layer** (atom, component, props, events, skeleton) — claims from `docs/ui/atom.md`, `docs/ui/component.md`, `docs/ui/props.md`, `docs/ui/events.md`, `docs/ui/skeleton.md`.\n- **State layer** (selectors, store, reducer, actions) — claims from `docs/state/selectors.md`, `docs/state/store.md`, `docs/state/reducer.md`, `docs/state/actions.md`; the selectors Short reuses the exact claim and measured figures (3 theme toggles, 3 re-renders, `createSelector` → 0, `toBe` not `toEqual`) from `skills/state-selectors/SKILL.md` and its LinkedIn/Instagram twins.\n- **Server layer** (SSR, container, protocol) — claims from `docs/server/ssr.md`, `docs/server/container.md`, `docs/server/protocol.md`.\n\nEvery Short points at one free, no-sign-up practice question on `elegantfrontend.training`, matching the brand's showcase rule. Nothing is posted; the file is held for CEO review.",
